  "url": "/css/css3_buttons_hover.asp",
  "title": "CSS Button Hover Effects",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "CSS Button Hover Effects"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This page covers CSS button hover effects, shadows, disabled states, and width."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Hoverable Buttons"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The CSS :hover pseudo-class is used to change the style of a button when you mouse over it."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Tip: Use the CSS transition-duration property to determine the\nspeed of the \"hover\" effect:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Green"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Blue"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Red"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Grey"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Black"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": ".button {\n  transition-duration: 0.4s;\n}\n\n.button:hover {\n\nbackground-color: #4CAF50; /* Green */\n  color: white;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_buttons_hover"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Buttons With Shadow"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The CSS box-shadow property\nis used to add a shadow to a button:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Shadow Button"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Shadow on hover"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": ".button1 {box-shadow:0 8px 16px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.6)}\n.button2:hover\n  {box-shadow:0 8px 16px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.6)}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_buttons_shadow"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Disabled Button"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The CSS opacity property\ncan be used to add transparency to a button (creates a\n\"disabled\" look)."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Tip: You can also add the cursor property with a value of\n\"not-allowed\", which will display a \"no parking sign\" when you mouse over the button:"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Disabled Button"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": ".disabledbtn {\n  opacity: 0.6;\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_buttons_disabled"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Button Width"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "By default, the size of a button is determined by its text content."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The CSS width property\ncan be used to define a specific width for a button."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Tip: Use pixels to set a fixed width, or percent for a responsive width (e.g. 50% of its parent element)."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "250px"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "50%"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "100%"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": ".button1 {width: 250px;}\n.button2 {width: 50%;}\n.button3 {width:\n100%;}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_buttons_width"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Button on Image"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "src": "https://www.w3schools.com/img_lights.jpg",
      "alt": "Snow"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Try it Yourself »"
    }
  ]
}
